Recommends: wl-clipboard, xclip
Suggests: x11-xkb-utils
Description: system-wide text expander (Linux port of KeyFlowMac)
 Replaces short triggers such as ";addr" with full snippets in any
 application, on X11 and Wayland. Keystrokes are read from /dev/input and the
 expansion is typed through /dev/uinput using the user's own keyboard layout.
 .
 Reading keyboards requires membership of the "input" group; see
 /usr/share/doc/keyflow/README.md.
